ok 1 - Codex manifest matches the repository version and has a native hook descriptor
ok 2 - Codex build-metadata stamp admits timestamp-and-OID and rejects malformed forms
ok 3 - descriptor uses quoted PLUGIN_ROOT with Windows parity for both routing families
ok 4 - Human override Git observation keeps a bounded cold-repository budget
ok 5 - lifecycle guard timeout derives from adapter budget and preserves recovery reserve
not ok 6 - Bash, apply_patch, Edit and Write each reach their intended guard family
not ok 7 - multiple Bash guard denials are aggregated into one Codex decision
not ok 8 - F1: codex adapter recognizes every push shape guard-push.mjs itself recognizes, via shared normalization
ok 9 - F1: the shared-normalization fix does not widen push detection to non-push commands
not ok 10 - F1 round 2: codex adapter recognizes the directPush and shellWrapperPush shapes guard-push.mjs itself recognizes
not ok 11 - F1 round 3: codex adapter recognizes the escaped-value and unrecognized-global-option push shapes lib/git-cmd.mjs now classifies
ok 12 - bounded rg-to-rg search filtering remains read-only without an override loop
not ok 13 - attended Human override admits only the exact next tool call and is then consumed
not ok 14 - ADR-0059 Decision 4: the continuation names the configured mode's own final step, in both modes
not ok 15 - Pipeline Author Repair selects one exact source root and consumes one patch
not ok 16 - local plugin-cache installation offers the human-gated HGO route without an audit retry loop
not ok 17 - a safe Bash local-plugin-install denial does not expose the original command outside HGO
not ok 18 - a secret-bearing Bash cross-repository-boundary denial never carries the secret verbatim
not ok 19 - override persistence failure remains a sanitized fail-closed denial
not ok 20 - Codex routes a documented Git override prefix to the Push-Gate's actual command
ok 21 - ordinary ungoverned shell commands do not start heavyweight guards
not ok 22 - runtime-only V3 targets activate lifecycle enforcement in the outer adapter
not ok 23 - Codex outer adapter admits only the exact pre-ready V4 recovery diagnostics
not ok 24 - Codex native cwd wins over a stale inherited CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR
not ok 25 - governed bootstrap can read only its loaded pipeline-start skill and current directory
not ok 26 - Codex adapter records a dispatched agent's receipt from the prescribed bootstrap before its first absolute-path Write
not ok 27 - outer Codex routing admits the exact bounded diagnostic pipeline while non-ready
not ok 28 - lifecycle readiness is additive and aggregates with existing write guards
not ok 29 - Codex adapter blocks consumer-to-source drift for Edit, apply_patch and plugin mutation
not ok 30 - existing write-guard warnings remain warnings in an ungoverned repository
not ok 31 - malformed, unsupported and incomplete tool inputs fail closed
not ok 32 - Codex adapter refuses recursive inventory of an external directory
ok 33 - GF-060/GF-064: an invalid lifecycle denial has no HGO route and never discloses a secret
ok 34 - GF-060/GF-094: an invalid lifecycle denial suppresses raw command and copy guidance
not ok 35 - NVA-CROSSREPOGUIDANCE-1: a cross-repository denial prints the TARGET repo in every ceremony line, and the printed plan command actually resolves there
not ok 36 - NVA-CROSSREPOGUIDANCE-1: an ordinary in-root denial still prints the session's own root, unchanged
not ok 37 - lifecycle-not-ready denial does not advertise a human override ceremony
